      "prepared_partitions": [
        {
          "context": "The tin was green; I have corrected my earlier description. Father taught me to remove a tyre, find the puncture, and wait for the glue before pressing on a rubber patch. I held a basin while he turned the inner tube through the water. We watched for bubbles. He let me try the patch after showing me once. I sometimes needed another attempt. I remember the basin and the patch, but I cannot remember the brand of glue or the exact year. The work happened in our shed. I have not described its colour or size, and I do not know what the weather was on those days. The maps I learned to read at school were a different memory. I do not know whether those lessons came before or after my first bicycle repair. I remember Father handing me the tin when it was time to put the tools away. I did not keep the tin, and I do not know where it is now.\n\nWe used rubber patches and glue to repair punctured inner tubes.\n\nThank you.\n\nI practised patching tyres beside Father. I sometimes asked him to check a patch.\n\nYes, that is what I remember.",
          "event_id": "27d9fc15-20c3-49f7-a0d3-2a5ed869fe43-messages-6",
