        "text": "The tin was green; I have corrected my earlier description. Father taught me to remove a tyre, find the puncture, and wait for the glue before pressing on a rubber patch. I held a basin while he turned the inner tube through the water. We watched for bubbles. He let me try the patch after showing me once. I sometimes needed another attempt. I remember the basin and the patch, but I cannot remember the brand of glue or the exact year. The work happened in our shed. I have not described its colour or size, and I do not know what the weather was on those days. The maps I learned to read at school were a different memory. I do not know whether those lessons came before or after my first bicycle repair. I remember Father handing me the tin when it was time to put the tools away. I did not keep the tin, and I do not know where it is now.",
        "version": "1"
      },
